Description: Forward and inverse Bayesian proxy system models for reconstructing
    bottom-water oxygen from benthic foraminiferal carbon-isotope offsets.
    Calibrated Bayesian linear regression and Gaussian-process models are
    distributed as lightweight posterior prediction assets, so ordinary use
    does not require refitting or a Stan installation. Functions propagate
    calibration, observation, and optional prior uncertainty.
